BAdam: "BAdam: A Memory Efficient Full Parameter Optimization Method for Large Language Models" (arXiv:2404.02827). The paper proposes "Block Coordinate Optimization with Adam" — block coordinate descent with Adam as the update rule within each block. Key points:

- BAdam is a block coordinate optimization method: parameters W are partitioned into blocks {θ_i}, and at each sub-iteration only one block is updated while the rest are frozen. Blocks are updated cyclically in order θ_1, ..., θ_D (sequential block update) — in one "block coordinate descent (BCD) epoch" all blocks are updated once. Between BCD epochs, the full dataset is reshuffled.
- The block update uses Adam's update rule but only over the active block's gradient, using the block-diagonal approximation of the Hessian / only gradients of the active block.
